==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|toe|rag}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[rag]] worn around the foot in place of a [[sock]].
#* '''1989''', {{w|Keith Bosley}}, translating Elias Lönnrot, ''The Kalevala'', XLIV:
#*: Steady old Väinämöinen / yonder crept with no shoes on / without '''toe-rags''' he tiptoed […].
# A [[tramp]] or [[vagrant]].
# A [[worthless]] or despicable person.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author={{w|J. K. Rowling}}|title=Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows|location=USA|publisher=Arthur A. Levine Books|page=674
|passage="I know James Potter's an arrogant '''toerag'''," she said, cutting across Snape.}}

